<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deportation and population transfer</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">Deportation</a> and population transfer describes the recurring imperial practice of forcibly moving conquered populations to suppress resistance, resettle land and supply labour. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> used it on a vast scale, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a> continued it with the Babylonian exile. It also appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>'s wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>'s treatment of subject peoples.</p></div>
